message: "If you use this model, please cite the software release."
title: "Climate Stress Test - Brazil 2026-2030"
version: "2.4.0"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chavatte
    given-names: João Carlos
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8432-4349"
date-released: "2026-09-16"
abstract: >
  Exploratory Agent-Based Model implemented in NetLogo to investigate
  systemic vulnerability and cascading interactions among synthetic
  municipalities under interacting climate, environmental, infrastructural,
  socioeconomic, and network-related stressors. The model is a stress-testing
  framework rather than an official climate forecast.
keywords:
  - agent-based modeling
  - NetLogo
  - climate risk
  - systemic risk
  - stress testing
  - cascading failures
  - complex networks
  - resilience
  - adaptation
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
